Firmware from ROCKNIX extra-firmware and Armada
Source: https://github.com/ROCKNIX/extra-firmware, commit 8834a0c80f5b24fee5ed9e18c1560dc48a6f1bd9,
SM8750/ directory; https://github.com/armada-os/armada, commit
d5f0724e610e91c2245dd12c692c0843b60a0068, system_files/usr/lib/firmware/qcom/sm8750/ayn/odin3/soccp.mbn

Files in this package taken from them (under /usr/lib/firmware):
  qcom/sm8750/ayn/odin3/* (ADSP and CDSP firmware, battery manager configuration, amplifier
  tuning; soccp.mbn from Armada, out of the Odin 3's Android modem partition),
  qcom/sm8750/SM8750-AYN-tplg.bin (audio topology), ath12k/WCN7860/hw2.0/* (Wi-Fi),
  qca/gngbtfw20.mbn and gngbtnv20.bin (Bluetooth)

These are proprietary firmware images, not Kettle Linux's, ROCKNIX's or Armada's own work: they
come from the device's vendor (AYN) and its chip vendor (Qualcomm), as ROCKNIX and Armada
collected them for their images. Neither repository states a licence for them, and the files
carry no licence text of their own.

Status: redistribution permission from the rights holders has NOT been recorded for Kettle
Linux. They are shipped pending that permission; this file grants no rights of any kind.

The other firmware in this package comes with its own licence files in this directory:
linux-firmware-qcom/ (Arch's linux-firmware package).
